<article class="env-lemma" id="02TQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02TQ">Lemma <span data-tag="02TQ">115.4.9</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a ring map. Let $f \in B$. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$A \to B$ is flat, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is a nonzerodivisor, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$A \to B/fB$ is flat. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then for every ideal $I \subset A$ the map $f : B/IB \to B/IB$ is injective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that $IB = I \otimes _ A B$ and $I(B/fB) = I \otimes _ A B/fB$ by the flatness of $B$ and $B/fB$ over $A$. In particular $IB/fIB \cong I \otimes _ A B/fB$ maps injectively into $B/fB$. Hence the result follows from the snake lemma applied to the diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ 0 \ar[r] &  I \otimes _ A B \ar[r] \ar[d]^ f &  B \ar[r] \ar[d]^ f &  B/IB \ar[r] \ar[d]^ f &  0 \\  0 \ar[r] &  I \otimes _ A B \ar[r] &  B \ar[r] &  B/IB \ar[r] &  0 }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       with exact rows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>